--- frame 3 (enter) ---
>a
.‸
--- frame 4 (b) ---
>a
.b‸
--- frame 5 (paste-end) ---
>a
.b‸
--- frame 6 (enter) ---
>a
.b

### TITLE ###
CtrlCDiscardsTheBufferWithoutEndingInput
### DESCRIPTION ###
Ctrl-C throws away what you were typing; the caller sees a discarded outcome
and prompts again. Result{Canceled} alone could not say this apart from EOF,
which is why the editor reports a typed outcome.
### PROMPT ###
>
### KEYS ###
"half typed"
ctrl-c
### VALUE ###
<canceled>
### OUTCOME ###
discarded
