### TITLE ###
CtrlDEndsInputOnlyWhenTheBufferIsEmpty
### DESCRIPTION ###
On an empty buffer Ctrl-D means "no more input". With text present it deletes
forward instead - ending a session because the cursor happened to sit at the
end would be a nasty surprise.
### PROMPT ###
>
### KEYS ###
"abc"
ctrl-a
ctrl-d
ctrl-d
ctrl-d
ctrl-d
### VALUE ###
<canceled>
### OUTCOME ###
eof
